WEBVTT

NOTE
Marginalia: editorial notes set beside the words they belong to.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:29.620
Kenneth Pitzer, president of Rice, had just introduced him. Rice Stadium, Houston: 12 September 1962, on a hot afternoon.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:01:03.360
The address was drafted with Ted Sorensen, the President’s speechwriter.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:35.360
The arithmetic: each year of the half-century stands for a thousand years of history.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:36.180
Mariner 2, launched 27 August 1962. It passed Venus on 14 December, the first spacecraft to fly by another planet.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:42.020
William Bradford, governor of Plymouth Colony, in his history Of Plymouth Plantation, begun in 1630.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:56.980
Charles Lindbergh’s solo flight from New York to Paris, May 1927.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:09:03.780
A football joke for the home crowd: Rice and the University of Texas met every year in the Southwest Conference.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:25.060
The Saturn C-1 flew as the Saturn I. The “advanced Saturn” with five F-1 engines became the Saturn V.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:23.680
The Atlas rocket that carried John Glenn’s Friendship 7, the first American orbital flight, 20 February 1962.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:42.420
Transit: the U.S. Navy’s satellite navigation system, a forerunner of GPS.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:51.640
TIROS, the first weather satellites, launched from 1960.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:52.780
The Manned Spacecraft Center opened in Houston in 1963. Since 1973 it has been the Johnson Space Center.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:32.670
The Moon’s average distance is about 239,000 miles (384,400 km).

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:43.010
Apollo 11 landed on 20 July 1969: six years and ten months after this speech.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:45.200
George Mallory was lost on Everest in June 1924. “Because it’s there” was his answer to a reporter in 1923.
